      "title": "Sweden’s PM resigns after centre-left bloc wins slim majority in election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/sweden-elections-prime-minister-resigns",
      "description": "<p>Ulf Kristersson has stood down from his post, paving way for Social Democrats leader to form a government</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/sweden\">Sweden</a>’s centre-right prime minister, Ulf Kristersson, has stood down, clearing the way for Magdalena Andersson, the Social Democrats leader, to attempt to form a government.</p><p>In a victory speech on Thursday, Andersson said the Swedish people had “voted for a new direction for our country, voted for unity and against division”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/sweden-elections-prime-minister-resigns\">Continue reading...</a>",
